","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--VqM2CfJm--/f_auto/v1763137628/posts/qfTWtwF4f?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-11-14T16:27:04.937Z"},{"id":"W0A0z8NYv","title":"Building a Page Builder via Content Modeling Best Practices in Strapi 5","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-a-page-builder-via-content-modeling-best-practices-in-strapi-5-w0a0z8nyv","summary":"Learn to build a scalable page builder using Strapi 5's content modeling features including collection types, single types, components, dynamic zones, and relations. The tutorial covers when to use each feature and demonstrates acceleration techniques with Strapi AI and Vercel v0.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--jQQDjlOq--/f_auto/v1758623140/posts/W0A0z8NYv?_a=BAMAK+ZW0","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-23T10:25:39.381Z"},{"id":"tieR9bf0R","title":"Digital Experience Platform Starter integrated with Strapi","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/digital-experience-platform-starter-integrated-with-strapi-tier9bf0r","summary":"An open-source starter kit combining Next.js and Strapi for building composable digital experience platforms. Features dynamic routing, modular page systems, API integration layer with NestJS, Tailwind styling, and ready-to-use content models. Designed for long-term scalability without vendor lock-in, suitable for content portals and customer support platforms.","image":null,"num_upvotes":14,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-09-04T11:31:38.341Z"},{"id":"CLEDhSTSw","title":"How Kenner Soft Service GmbH Built a Military Informational Portal with Strapi","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-kenner-soft-service-gmbh-built-a-military-informational-portal-with-strapi-cledhstsw","summary":"Kenner Soft Service GmbH successfully developed and deployed a secure military training portal for Ukrainian citizens within one month. The project utilized Strapi as the content management system, Vue.js for the frontend, and Cloudflare Stream for video delivery, demonstrating how modern web technologies can be rapidly deployed for critical government and defense applications.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--KXbghH-T--/f_auto/v1753955124/posts/CLEDhSTSw?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-31T09:45:23.661Z"},{"id":"T8lRJO4aq","title":"\u26a1\ufe0f Lightning Fast Building with Strapi & Astro","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/lightning-fast-building-with-strapi-astro-t8lrjo4aq","summary":"A guide demonstrating how to combine Astro static site generator with Strapi headless CMS to create fast-loading, SEO-optimized content websites. Covers integration techniques using Astro Strapi Loader, Blocks Field functionality, and starter kit implementation for improved performance.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--pFTDDrbn--/f_auto/v1752082070/posts/T8lRJO4aq?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-07-09T17:27:23.671Z"},{"id":"3YlrSVj4r","title":"Building faster content-driven sites with Astro","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/building-faster-content-driven-sites-with-astro-3ylrsvj4r","summary":"Matt Kane, Astro's Framework Lead and former Gatsby core maintainer, explains why Astro is superior for building content-driven websites. The presentation covers Astro's performance advantages and positioning as the optimal choice for content-focused web development.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--0mXc0g4L--/f_auto/v1750445001/posts/3YlrSVj4r?_a=BAMClqZW0","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-06-20T18:43:08.884Z"},{"id":"ZpZ5z5bHF","title":"Build a Google Meet Clone with Strapi 5 and Next.js - Part 1 & 2","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-a-google-meet-clone-with-strapi-5-and-next-js---part-1-2-zpz5z5bhf","summary":"Learn to build a Google Meet clone using Next.js and Strapi 5 in this tutorial series. Key features include real-time video conferencing, screen sharing, chat messaging, meeting scheduling, and user presence indicators. Access the example code on GitHub and start building with Strapi 5 today!","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--i-tJWFoO--/f_auto/v1740134615/posts/ZpZ5z5bHF","num_upvotes":3,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-21T10:43:30.159Z"},{"id":"Ktw5vvpxT","title":"React Router 7 With Strapi 5 is Awesome","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/react-router-7-with-strapi-5-is-awesome-ktw5vvpxt","summary":"React Router 7 has been released and this integration guide explains how to use it with Strapi 5. A complementary video is available to provide additional insights.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--E67RFher--/f_auto/v1736171607/posts/dfQhyYq3t","num_upvotes":12,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2025-01-07T11:11:32.997Z"},{"id":"UM7GZ2qgi","title":"Build a Real-Time Voting System with Strapi & Instant DB: Part 2","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/build-a-real-time-voting-system-with-strapi-instant-db-part-2-um7gz2qgi","summary":"Learn how to create the frontend of a real-time voting system using Next.js and integrate it with a Strapi 5 backend. This tutorial covers setting up a user store with Zustand, utilizing REST APIs for authentication and poll management, building responsive components, and deploying to platforms like Strapi Cloud and Netlify.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--yGsFyJx3--/f_auto/v1731083817/posts/UM7GZ2qgi","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-11-08T16:36:56.904Z"},{"id":"XDR79mQEt","title":"Image Upload to Strapi via REST API with Next.js and Postman","url":"","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/image-upload-to-strapi-via-rest-api-with-next-js-and-postman-xdr79mqet","summary":"Learn how to upload single or multiple images to Strapi using Next.js and Postman. The tutorial covers linking images to entries, mastering image uploads with the API Controller, updating image file information, and deleting images.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--LPaCuDt5--/f_auto/v1730295554/posts/XDR79mQEt","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2024-10-30T13:39:11.971Z"}],"similar_handles":["frontend_developer","shamundev","nextaitool","proflead","microsaasexamples"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","xai","hamelhusain","hwchase17","skirano"],"similar":[{"id":"5a4b697d-2783-4c1b-9477-c593ebb06ef0","handle":"frontend_developer","name":"Frontend developer","is_squad":true,"x":-8.9388,"y":8.7535,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":23,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--ebMZ400Y--/f_auto/v1736964764/squads/5a4b697d-2783-4c1b-9477-c593ebb06ef0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.344719,"median_upvotes":1.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.021739,"avg_read_time":1.304348,"tag_diversity":1.869565},"top_tags_preview":[["webdev",16],["react",6],["nextjs",6]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[2.6471,9.5],"cadence_depth":[-7.7647,-8.7206],"hype_variety":[5.1471,1.4412],"title_style":[-7.8971,-6.6176]}},{"id":"shamundev","handle":"shamundev","name":"Ido Shamun","is_squad":false,"x":-8.7298,"y":8.5372,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":13,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/4df9590bfe494592ae55932a66d18369","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.964764,"median_upvotes":10.0,"author_present_share":1.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":3.461538,"tag_diversity":1.384615},"top_tags_preview":[["startup",4],["leadership",3],["webdev",2]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[8.5735,9.0],"cadence_depth":[-9.2059,-5.8382],"hype_variety":[-5.2206,-4.3235],"title_style":[-5.1765,-2.2647]}},{"id":"e00b4499-9e40-4271-99c6-068a74910b4f","handle":"nextaitool","name":"Next AI Tool","is_squad":true,"x":-8.7236,"y":8.6017,"cluster_id":2,"posts_collected":80,"image":